---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Git Commit Message Assistant — Max Vogt">
  <main id="top" class="page-container">
    <header class="section-pad fade-up">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-6">
        <label class="toggle text-base">
          <a class="text-[1.25rem] font-semibold text-[var(--color-text)] hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]" href="/">Max.</a>
          <input type="checkbox" aria-label="Toggle dark mode" data-theme-toggle />
          <span class="toggle-icons" aria-hidden="true">
            <span class="toggle-icon icon-moon">◑</span>
          </span>
        </label>
        <nav class="flex items-center gap-8 text-base">
          <a class="nav-link transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]" href="/">Work</a>
          <a class="nav-link transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]" href="/about">About</a>
          <a
            class="nav-link transition-colors duration-200 hover:text-[var(--color-primary)]"
            href="https://www.instagram.com/maaxvogt/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            Fun
          </a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="section-pad fade-up delay-1">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <h1 class="text-[clamp(2.8rem,6vw,4.6rem)]">Git Commit Message Assistant</h1>
        <p class="text-lg text-muted max-w-[52rem]">
          A VS Code extension that analyzes code changes and suggests concise, structured commit
          messages to improve readability, consistency, and collaboration in software teams. The
          project focuses on developer experience, clarity, and practical adoption rather than
          automated commit generation.
        </p>
        <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3 text-sm">
          <div>
            <p class="text-muted uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">Role</p>
            <p>Software Engineer / Tooling Engineer</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-muted uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">Team</p>
            <p>Solo project</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="text-muted uppercase tracking-[0.2em]">Duration</p>
            <p>~4–6 weeks (design, implementation, publishing, iteration)</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad fade-up delay-2">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Context</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            Commit messages are a critical yet often neglected part of software collaboration.
            Inconsistent or low-quality messages reduce traceability, slow down code reviews, and
            weaken long-term maintainability.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            This project was motivated by the observation that while teams care deeply about code
            quality, commit quality is rarely enforced or supported by tooling. The goal was to create
            a lightweight assistant that integrates directly into the developer workflow without
            adding friction.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Technical Approach</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            The extension is designed around a workflow-first and deterministic core, ensuring
            predictable behavior and developer trust.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted font-semibold">Change analysis</p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            The extension inspects staged Git diffs to understand the scope and nature of code changes.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted font-semibold">Structured message generation</p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Suggested commit messages follow a clear structure (type, scope, summary), encouraging best
            practices without enforcing rigid rules.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted font-semibold">AI-assisted refinement (optional)</p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            AI is used as an assistive layer to improve phrasing and clarity, while developers retain
            full control over the final message.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted font-semibold">VS Code–native integration</p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            Built using the VS Code Extension API, the assistant integrates seamlessly into existing
            Git workflows.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            The design intentionally avoids fully automated commits, keeping developers in the decision loop.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Impact & Adoption Signals</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            Despite being a developer tool, the project shows clear indicators of practical value:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-muted space-y-2">
            <li>Improved commit message consistency across repositories</li>
            <li>Reduced cognitive load when writing commits for larger or mixed changes</li>
            <li>Positive feedback from users regarding readability and usefulness</li>
            <li>Published and maintained as a real VS Code extension, not a prototype</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-muted">
            The project demonstrates how small, focused tools can meaningfully improve team workflows.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Learning and Growth</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted">
            Building the Git Commit Message Assistant strengthened my experience in developer tooling
            and UX-driven engineering:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 text-muted space-y-2">
            <li>Designing tools that developers trust and willingly adopt</li>
            <li>Balancing automation with developer control</li>
            <li>Working with Git internals and diff representations</li>
            <li>Publishing, versioning, and maintaining a public VS Code extension</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-muted">
            It reinforced that developer experience is a product discipline, not just a UI concern.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="case-row">
        <h2 class="case-title">Takeaway</h2>
        <div class="case-body">
          <p class="text-muted font-semibold">
            Great developer tools don’t replace judgment — they amplify it.
          </p>
          <p class="text-muted">
            This project shows how thoughtful automation, when embedded directly into existing
            workflows, can improve collaboration and code quality without disrupting developer autonomy.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="mt-16 text-right">
        <a href="#top" class="nav-link text-base">Back to Top ↑</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-pad">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <h2>Let's get in touch</h2>
        <p class="text-muted">
          HMU for work, coffee, or if you just want to talk.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-6 text-sm">
          <a
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-transparent transition-colors duration-200 hover:border-[var(--color-primary)]"
            href="https://github.com/maaxvogt/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>
          <a
            class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-transparent transition-colors duration-200 hover:border-[var(--color-primary)]"
            href="mailto:mavoxgt@gmail.com"
          >
            Mail
          </a>
        </div>
        <p class="text-sm text-muted">Designed and coded by Max Vogt</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</Layout>
